From 69848a4d9b92c580bb00e133759955e5fdd2e3a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 16:37:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arifi-sync: x1i-reword table - one commit per win carries the
 number

The first table gave every commit of a release-ledger win that win's number, and Table 2
non-results their result text. A dry run then showed protected-win validate failing 28 times:
each such commit reads as a landed, unregistered measured win. That claims measurements nobody
took per commit. Now only the win's first-listed ledger commit carries the number (12 rows);
the other commits of a win, the protected-wins registration commits and the Table 2 rows say
"UNMEASURED on its own - ..." with the win named (25 rows); 1 row keeps a number from its own
subject; 20 stay UNMEASURED.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - release engineering for this fork; no upstream origin exists.
Origin: release-prep (HQ82)
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - release tooling only. Dry run on a scratch clone of release/prep @ d3958ae2ed: 63 commits replayed, 58 reworded.
